# fixedbugs, defect 2044, 2026-10-13, the defect's own name.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own that declares `int64_t` another
# way, `typedef long int64_t;` on this Mac or `int int64_t;` anywhere, was
# told `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at exit 2: clang's
# note points at `heroes_runtime.h`'s `typedef __INT64_TYPE__ int64_t;`, the
# type declared again as C11 6.7p3 allows, and a note in the runtime's files
# was the compiler's (defect 360's rule).
#
# FIX: a note at the runtime's line declaring a name of `<stdint.h>` again
# as C does, read from the line itself (`cli/standard_name.hero`), is told as
# C's own, and the header is refused at its line 1, exit 1. The header would
# be refused beside any `<stdint.h>` just the same.

extern "fixedbugs-2044-a-header-that-declares-int64-t-as-a-variable-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function seven() -> i32

function main()
    print(seven())
